              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "missdrea"
            },
            "reviewBody": "yum. i also used a full cup of barley. i threw everything in my slow cooker for 1 hour on high then low for 4 hours. i ended up adding some water halfway through since i used more barley. i loved the creamy consistency the added barley gave the soup. this made a ton so i froze some to give away to family",
            "datePublished": "2010-02-11T14:53:24.027Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Liz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great soup. 1 1/2 hours is way too long for cooking it though. It was pretty mushy, although tasty. I used half chicken broth &amp; half water. I will cook for 1 hr next time, adding the cabbage in the last 20-30 minutes for some crunchiness.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-01T14:25:04.493Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mom_v_3"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! I used one box of campbell's reduced salt and one regular chicken broth. I also added 3 cloves of minced garlic, a pinch of thyme and 3 bay leaves (remove prior to serving) for a hint of extra flavor. For those of you who felt it was salty.... try adding the ham in the last 15 mins of cooking, not only will less of the salt from the ham leach into the soup, the ham won't toughen up or become a weird pale color. Thanks for the post.",
            "datePublished": "2007-10-29T10:26:14.477Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kim"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Best soup I've ever made! We used sausage instead of ham and sautéed the veggies and browned the meat before throwing the soup together. Excellent.",
            "datePublished": "2015-10-06T18:03:02.590Z"
          },
          {
