            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PammyJ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a very good recipe. I guess you could say we cut it in half and adapted to our taste.\r\n\r\nI used 1 lb of chopped smoked sausage that I sauteed with the onions, celery and carrots. Added 3 cans of chicken broth along with 1 can of cream of chicken soup along with approx 2 cups of water. We also added bay leaves and fresh basil along with fresh ground pepper and a bit of salt. This mixture simmered on low heat for about 30 - 45 minutes, stirring every couple of minutes. Added 1/2 large head of shredded cabbage and cooked until tender.",
            "datePublished": "2004-03-14T16:21:38.293Z"
